{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-02T21:54:15.879Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Source changes**\n- `src/cli/plan-queue.ts` — `prepareQueueSelection` throws `CommandError(refusal message)` instead of printing and setting `process.exitCode = 1`; the incomplete-coverage notice still prints and a ready selection is still returned.\n- `src/cli/plan.ts` — a non-zero planner exit code throws `new CommandError('', { exitCode })` after `recordPlanExited`.\n- `src/cli/index.ts` — the `plan` and `serve` actions rethrow a `CommandError` unchanged and wrap any other error as `CommandError('Error: <message>')`, no longer touching `process.exitCode`.\n\n**Tests**\n- Added `tests/plan-command-error.test.ts` covering direct `prepareQueueSelection` refusal/notice, direct `planCommand` exit code, and the `plan`/`serve` CLI paths through `runCliCaptured` (queue refusal, planner exit code, other plan error, failing serve).\n- Updated `tests/plan-telemetry.test.ts`, `tests/queue-budget.test.ts`, `tests/queue-plan.test.ts` to assert thrown `CommandError`s, and `tests/codex/plan.test.ts`'s subprocess runner to map the thrown error onto the child's exit code.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify: `node --import tsx --test tests/plan-command-error.test.ts` — 7/7 pass.\n- Proposal verify: `pnpm verify` — exit 0 (3127 + 94 tests, 0 fail), typecheck, build, and lint all clean.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/141-commands-report-failure/.run/results/5.md`."}}
